  <prompt>
    Revert the DailyBriefingCollector membership-resolver bypass (lines 216-248) so candidate-set resolution routes through IMembershipResolverService again (relying on the R7 root-cause fix to MembershipFieldDiscoveryService that synthesizes Owner/Customer targets). Re-flip the pinned test DailyBriefingCollectorTests.CollectAsync_OwnershipGate_UsesOwnerScopedQueryExpressions_ResolverBypassed (line 238) — which PR #558 deliberately rewrote to ASSERT the bypass — so it re-asserts resolver ROUTING. Add a collaborator smoke test proving a sprk_assignedattorney1 user sees an assigned, non-owned matter in the briefing. Per FR-C4.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in the DailyBriefing collector, IMembershipResolverService / MembershipFieldDiscoveryService membership resolution, and Dataverse polymorphic Owner attribute metadata.
  </role>

  <goal>
    DailyBriefingCollector resolves event/matter/project candidate IDs via IMembershipResolverService (the bypass at 216-248, including the direct ResolveOwnedIdsAsync owner-only fan-out at 236-239, is removed and replaced with the resolver-routed path). The pinned test at line 238 now asserts resolver routing (not bypass) and passes. A new collaborator smoke test asserts that a sprk_assignedattorney1 user sees a matter they are assigned to but do not own. No regression for the owner-scoped case. BFF builds 0 errors; publish size reported per NFR-01.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      R7 W12 introduced an Owner-only bypass (comment at lines 216-235) because the resolver returned 0 rows for Owner-based membership fields — LookupAttributeMetadata is sealed and OwnerAttributeMetadata doesn't inherit from it. R7 ALSO root-cause-fixed MembershipFieldDiscoveryService.ProjectLookupAttributeRows to synthesize Owner/Customer targets. With the root cause fixed, the bypass now silently under-scopes: collaborators (assigned attorneys/paralegals) never appear in the briefing. PR #558 deliberately rewrote the test to assert the bypass so that removing it forces this conversation. See notes/inbound-from-r7/03 item 1.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Narrators/DailyBriefingCollector.cs</file>
      <file>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Ai/Narrators/DailyBriefingCollectorTests.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-daily-update-service-r5/notes/inbound-from-r7/03-code-review-followups.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Remove the bypass at DailyBriefingCollector.cs lines 216-248: replace the direct ResolveOwnedIdsAsync(...) owner-only fan-out (236-239) with resolver-routed candidate resolution through IMembershipResolverService (the ResolveMembershipsSafelyAsync path the bypass comment says to revert to). Update the log line at 246-248 to drop the "resolver bypass — R7 W12" wording.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Re-flip the pinned test at DailyBriefingCollectorTests.cs:238 (CollectAsync_OwnershipGate_UsesOwnerScopedQueryExpressions_ResolverBypassed). It currently asserts the bypass; rewrite it to assert the collector ROUTES through IMembershipResolverService. Rename the test if the "_ResolverBypassed" suffix no longer describes it. This is a deliberate re-flip of a PR #558 pin — expected, not accidental.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Add a collaborator smoke test: a systemUser who is a sprk_assignedattorney1 (collaborator, NOT owner) of a matter sees that matter in the collected briefing candidate set. The test must fail against the old bypass and pass against the resolver-routed path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST NOT regress the owner-scoped case: a user who owns a matter/project/event still sees it. Keep or add a test asserting owner-scoped inclusion still holds.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Do not widen the AI boundary; IMembershipResolverService is an existing dependency of the collector — reuse it, do not inject new AI-internal types.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE.md-§10">BFF-touching task: state the placement decision (change stays inside the existing collector; no new service/DI), run dotnet publish -c Release, report compressed size + diff vs ~49.63 MB baseline (incl PDBs), confirm no new HIGH-severity CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

