  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Run /conflict-check for Services/Ai/Narrators/DailyBriefingCollector.cs against the r2-core worktree (root §7); register the touch in projects/INDEX.md.</step>
    <step order="2">Read DailyBriefingCollector.cs 205-280 and confirm the resolver-routed helper the bypass comment says to revert to (ResolveMembershipsSafelyAsync). Replace the bypass fan-out (236-239) with resolver-routed candidate resolution for events/matters/projects; update the log line (246-248).</step>
    <step order="3">Verify MembershipFieldDiscoveryService's R7 root-cause fix (Owner/Customer target synthesis) is present so the resolver returns rows for Owner-based fields. If it is NOT present, escalate (see escalation) rather than restoring the bypass.</step>
    <step order="4">Re-flip DailyBriefingCollectorTests.cs:238 to assert resolver routing; rename if the _ResolverBypassed suffix is now wrong. Update fixture setup per test-fixture-contracts.md (inspect fixture config/claims/mocks first if the resolver returns unexpected rows).</step>
    <step order="5">Add the collaborator smoke test (sprk_assignedattorney1 user sees a non-owned assigned matter) and an owner-scoped regression test (owner still sees owned records).</step>
    <step order="6">Build: dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ (0 errors). Run: dotnet test for the collector test project; confirm re-flipped + smoke + owner tests pass.</step>
    <step order="7">Run dotnet publish -c Release, report compressed size + diff vs 49.63 MB baseline (incl PDBs); dotnet list package --vulnerable → no new HIGH CVE.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md task 033 → completed; record any deviations in notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If reverting the bypass reintroduces a real reason it existed — the resolver still returns 0 rows for Owner-based fields (the R7 root-cause fix is absent or incomplete), or a measurable performance/correctness regression appears — STOP and escalate per root CLAUDE.md §6.5 (ADR/decision conflict). Do NOT silently keep the bypass; surface the conflict and choose a resolution path.</trigger>
  </escalation>

